00:14:54,184 --> 00:14:57,229
- [Su-ho yelps]
- [laughs] You rude little prick.

250
00:14:58,230 --> 00:15:00,524
- [knife clicks]
- [Gil-su laughs]

251
00:15:00,608 --> 00:15:01,650
Let's go.

252
00:15:10,618 --> 00:15:12,453
[engines revving]

253
00:15:12,536 --> 00:15:15,456
- [tires screeching]
- [horns honking]

254
00:15:24,214 --> 00:15:25,466
Are you okay, Su-ho-ya?

255
00:15:27,676 --> 00:15:29,553
- [Su-ho] Not at all. Fuck.
- [Beom-seok] Hold on.

256
00:15:29,637 --> 00:15:30,512
[Su-ho] Okay.

257
00:15:31,263 --> 00:15:32,640
[groans]

258
00:15:32,723 --> 00:15:34,391
- [Beom-seok] What do we do?
- [Su-ho sighs]

259
00:15:34,975 --> 00:15:37,645
They can't do anything. Ow, shit.

260
00:15:41,357 --> 00:15:43,692
I don't know why it's not starting.
They said it'd run.

261
00:15:43,776 --> 00:15:45,361
- [boy 1] Hey, yeah.
- [ringing tone]

262
00:15:50,324 --> 00:15:51,450
Kids are coming out.

263
00:15:53,077 --> 00:15:55,079
[tense music playing]

264
00:15:58,082 --> 00:15:59,625
[boy 2] Who is this? All right.

265
00:16:00,125 --> 00:16:01,460
[boy 3 spits]

266
00:16:05,339 --> 00:16:06,507
[laughs]

267
00:16:06,590 --> 00:16:09,677
- I'll go with you when you go.
- I'll look over it again.

268
00:16:17,101 --> 00:16:18,018
[boy 4] Is that him?

269
00:16:20,145 --> 00:16:21,146
Hey.

270
00:16:27,403 --> 00:16:28,988
[boy 5] We're just hanging out.

271
00:16:29,738 --> 00:16:31,991
[boy 6] Yeah, I could
really eat something.

272
00:16:32,074 --> 00:16:33,450
[boy 5] What's he lookin' at?

273
00:16:33,534 --> 00:16:35,911
- [coughs]
- [laughs] Yeah.

274
00:16:36,745 --> 00:16:38,747
[tense music continues]

275
00:16:47,006 --> 00:16:49,008
[horn beeping]

276
00:16:51,593 --> 00:16:52,720
[lock bleeps]

277
00:16:59,518 --> 00:17:00,853
[music fades]

278
00:17:04,606 --> 00:17:05,649
[phone bleeps]

279
00:17:05,733 --> 00:17:06,984
[ringing tone]

280
00:17:09,653 --> 00:17:10,779
[Yeong-i] <i>Hello?</i>

281
00:17:11,405 --> 00:17:12,823
Let's meet somewhere.

282
00:17:20,414 --> 00:17:22,041
- [door opens]
- [shop bell rings]

283
00:17:25,085 --> 00:17:27,087
[muzak playing]

284
00:17:37,014 --> 00:17:39,308
[sighs] That guy.

285
00:17:39,391 --> 00:17:40,684
What does he do?

286
00:17:41,185 --> 00:17:42,186
Who?

287
00:17:44,938 --> 00:17:45,981
Oh.

288
00:17:47,024 --> 00:17:48,192
Gil-su?

289
00:17:49,485 --> 00:17:50,319
[smacks lips]

290
00:17:50,402 --> 00:17:53,989
[sighs] That guy lets us crash
and gives us a job.

291
00:17:55,032 --> 00:17:57,409
- What kind?
- [Yeong-i] You know, this and that.

292
00:17:58,660 --> 00:17:59,912
Why do you care?

293
00:18:04,166 --> 00:18:05,167
[sighs]

294
00:18:06,251 --> 00:18:07,961
I shouldn't be saying this.

295
00:18:11,381 --> 00:18:13,801
Just watch your back 'cause he's trash.

296
00:18:14,426 --> 00:18:15,302
[tense music playing]

297
00:18:15,385 --> 00:18:18,472
[Yeong-i] He wasn't lying when he said
he killed people for money.

298
00:18:19,556 --> 00:18:22,142
He has gangster connections. Real ones.

299
00:18:23,936 --> 00:18:26,522
He's money-crazy. He's not even human.

300
00:18:27,689 --> 00:18:28,524
So what?

301
00:18:28,607 --> 00:18:31,360
Give him whatever money you have,
even if it's half.

302
00:18:32,111 --> 00:18:33,362
[Si-eun] Otherwise?

303
00:18:34,530 --> 00:18:36,115
What happens if I don't?

304
00:18:37,908 --> 00:18:38,784
[sighs]

305
00:18:42,496 --> 00:18:43,664
You're fucked.

306
00:18:46,333 --> 00:18:48,460
You'll be fucked like the rest of us.

307
00:18:57,594 --> 00:18:58,720
Will it be done?

308
00:19:00,139 --> 00:19:01,181
[Yeong-i] What?

309
00:19:04,059 --> 00:19:05,102
If he gets paid?

310
00:19:10,983 --> 00:19:12,734
- [Yeong-i] Hmm.
- Will you be okay?

311
00:19:18,657 --> 00:19:20,033
[music stops]

312
00:19:23,620 --> 00:19:25,164
[suspenseful music playing]

313
00:19:50,898 --> 00:19:52,649
[quiet clattering]

314
00:20:05,287 --> 00:20:06,830
[exhales]

315
00:20:14,129 --> 00:20:15,631
[Su-ho yawns]

316
00:20:17,007 --> 00:20:18,800
Why? What's going on?

317
00:20:19,927 --> 00:20:20,928
What is it?

318
00:20:22,429 --> 00:20:24,640
Man, I'm hungry. Ugh.

319
00:20:27,142 --> 00:20:29,519
CHEMISTRY LAB

320
00:20:32,189 --> 00:20:33,398
[Su-ho yawns]

321
00:20:34,441 --> 00:20:37,236
[sighs] I'll do it. I'll take care of it.

322
00:20:39,112 --> 00:20:41,406
- Hmm?
- It's been three days.

323
00:20:42,741 --> 00:20:44,368
[unzips bag]

324
00:20:46,995 --> 00:20:48,247
Fifteen million won.

325
00:20:50,582 --> 00:20:52,376
Once he has it, it'll end.

326
00:20:54,670 --> 00:20:55,712
[Su-ho] What's this?

327
00:20:57,130 --> 00:20:59,091
Um, it's from my parents.

328
00:20:59,174 --> 00:21:01,134
Are you kidding me? Huh?

329
00:21:01,635 --> 00:21:03,762
Your parents just gave you this?

330
00:21:04,513 --> 00:21:05,389
Where'd you get it?

331
00:21:06,598 --> 00:21:09,893
- Why does that even that matter?
- [Su-ho] Where'd you get it?

332
00:21:11,603 --> 00:21:12,604
Where's it from?

333
00:21:16,024 --> 00:21:17,442
I sold my father's watch.

334
00:21:17,943 --> 00:21:20,654
He was handing it down to me anyway, so…

335
00:21:20,737 --> 00:21:22,990
What an idiot. Huh?

336
00:21:23,991 --> 00:21:26,743
Why give money to that asshole?
We can just call the police.

337
00:21:26,827 --> 00:21:27,869
[sighs]

338
00:21:29,079 --> 00:21:31,498
Take this and get your watch back.

339
00:21:32,749 --> 00:21:35,335
They told us that going to the police
wouldn't do us any good.

340
00:21:36,378 --> 00:21:37,629
Beom-seok-a.

341
00:21:39,256 --> 00:21:40,590
Thanks a lot.

342
00:21:41,341 --> 00:21:43,719
But I'll handle it. Don't worry about it.

343
00:21:43,802 --> 00:21:46,221
[Su-ho] How the hell
are you gonna handle it?

344
00:21:46,305 --> 00:21:47,681
Let's just report it.

345
00:21:47,764 --> 00:21:50,058
Yeah, I'm gonna do that.

346
00:21:57,941 --> 00:22:00,902
That asshole makes
runaway kids do jobs for him.

347
00:22:02,029 --> 00:22:03,405
PROMISSORY NOTE

348
00:22:03,488 --> 00:22:06,491
Do you know about Free Money?
It's popular with high school kids.

349
00:22:07,951 --> 00:22:10,537
- What? What's that?
- A gambling site.

350
00:22:11,121 --> 00:22:14,333
It gives you 50,000 won as soon
as you join, so it's called Free Money.

351
00:22:15,876 --> 00:22:18,211
Gil-su's partner runs it overseas.

352
00:22:18,920 --> 00:22:20,172
Everything's rigged.

353
00:22:20,922 --> 00:22:22,466
They let you win the first few rounds.

354
00:22:22,549 --> 00:22:24,634
<i>You end up making tens of millions of won.</i>

355
00:22:24,718 --> 00:22:27,429
<i>- False hope. They let you keep winning.</i>
- [phone chimes]

356
00:22:28,388 --> 00:22:32,100
That's when it happens.
You begin to lose everything that you won.

357
00:22:33,310 --> 00:22:35,395
- [sad sound effect]
- [Yeong-i] <i>Nothing is chance.</i>

358
00:22:35,896 --> 00:22:39,524
<i>Their balance of tens of millions of won</i>
<i>suddenly drops to zero.</i>

359
00:22:39,608 --> 00:22:41,151
They go nuts.

360
00:22:42,736 --> 00:22:45,697
So they keep gambling,
trying to win back what they lost.

361
00:22:46,198 --> 00:22:49,785
But how do they keep gambling?
They lost their money.

362
00:22:49,868 --> 00:22:50,702
[bleep]

363
00:22:53,580 --> 00:22:55,415
[Yeong-i] <i>Gil-su has</i>
<i>membership information,</i>

364
00:22:55,499 --> 00:22:58,001
<i>so he approaches them</i>
<i>and offers a private loan.</i>

365
00:23:01,129 --> 00:23:03,882
<i>All these kids obviously</i>
<i>can't repay the debt they owe,</i>

366
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:06,176
<i>so they bring collateral.</i>

367
00:23:06,843 --> 00:23:09,429
<i>A few days ago,</i>
<i>someone even brought their mom's car.</i>

368
00:23:11,306 --> 00:23:14,726
<i>He basically makes the kids steal money</i>
<i>and stuff from their parents.</i>

369
00:23:16,144 --> 00:23:19,648
[Si-eun] <i>Then he takes out private loans</i>
<i>using the kids' bank accounts.</i>

370
00:23:20,357 --> 00:23:22,567
<i>He makes them do dead drops for drugs.</i>

371
00:23:22,651 --> 00:23:25,946
Gets them involved in crimes,
keeping them trapped.

372
00:23:27,572 --> 00:23:30,742
<i>Their housing has ledgers,</i>
<i>contracts, even illegal drugs.</i>

373
00:23:30,826 --> 00:23:33,120
All we need to do is bring
the police over there.

374
00:23:33,912 --> 00:23:34,913
[Beom-seok sighs]

375
00:23:36,289 --> 00:23:37,791
How'd you know about all that?

376
00:23:39,418 --> 00:23:40,752
Did you Google it?

377
00:23:44,172 --> 00:23:46,508
Uh, I… just know.

378
00:23:47,968 --> 00:23:48,885
[sighs]

379
00:23:50,387 --> 00:23:53,849
[Su-ho] Well, let's do Si-eun's great plan
right after we get something to eat.

380
00:23:53,932 --> 00:23:57,060
Okay? I'm so hungry, I could die!

381
00:23:59,729 --> 00:24:01,189
[menacing music playing]

382
00:24:05,735 --> 00:24:07,195
Hey, one sec.

383
00:24:10,907 --> 00:24:11,908
[Si-eun] Why?

384
00:24:15,954 --> 00:24:18,123
I'll, um… go by myself.

385
00:24:19,374 --> 00:24:20,333
What?

386
00:24:22,252 --> 00:24:25,922
Hey, like you said, if the ledgers
and drugs are at their place,

387
00:24:26,006 --> 00:24:28,800
office, or whatever,
we have to bring the police over there.

388
00:24:29,801 --> 00:24:31,511
Yeah. I'll call them right now.

389
00:24:31,595 --> 00:24:35,140
No, dude. You have to catch them there.
Photos won't do any good.

390
00:24:36,850 --> 00:24:39,811
So I'll go there first
and send you the address.

391
00:24:40,479 --> 00:24:43,273
Come with the police. I'll stall for time.

392
00:24:43,356 --> 00:24:45,442
Hey, you can't go by yourself.

393
00:24:46,860 --> 00:24:50,280
I'm still the toughest guy
at Byuksan High. You don't trust me?

394
00:24:51,448 --> 00:24:54,034
It's all right, 'kay? Bye.

395
00:24:57,704 --> 00:24:58,872
[sighs]

396
00:24:59,498 --> 00:25:02,083
[boy 1] Yeah, I think
I'm maybe gonna ask her out tonight.

397
00:25:05,045 --> 00:25:05,921
[Gil-su] Hey!

398
00:25:06,963 --> 00:25:08,757
You Three Musketeers disbanded?

399
00:25:10,926 --> 00:25:13,595
[Su-ho] Hey, we're not
a bunch of dicks like you.

400
00:25:13,678 --> 00:25:14,888
We only need one.

401
00:25:14,971 --> 00:25:18,225
[sighs] Stop talking shit
and hand it over. Right now.

402
00:25:19,351 --> 00:25:20,727
Before I do that,

403
00:25:21,895 --> 00:25:23,188
let's have a word, man to man.

404
00:25:23,271 --> 00:25:24,689
God… [splutters]

405
00:25:26,775 --> 00:25:28,026
You don't have it, do you?

406
00:25:28,818 --> 00:25:30,028
[chuckles]

407
00:25:31,029 --> 00:25:32,906
I have something better. Hmm?

408
00:25:34,115 --> 00:25:35,867
[sighs] I mean, here's the thing.

409
00:25:36,576 --> 00:25:39,913
<i>Hyeong, </i>I'm the top dog in this school.

410
00:25:41,873 --> 00:25:43,875
There's a way I can help you out here.

411
00:25:43,959 --> 00:25:46,920
That gambling website of yours
can make a lot more money.

412
00:25:47,003 --> 00:25:48,547
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

413
00:25:50,882 --> 00:25:51,967
How'd you know that?

414
00:25:56,137 --> 00:25:57,222
Him.

415
00:25:57,847 --> 00:25:59,432
His cousin is in my class.

416
00:25:59,933 --> 00:26:02,644
- He showed me the website before.
- Aah.

417
00:26:02,727 --> 00:26:04,187
- [Su-ho] Mm-hmm.
- Aah.

418
00:26:07,315 --> 00:26:10,151
Everybody gets a voucher
for 50,000 won when they join.

419
00:26:10,986 --> 00:26:15,532
Instead of giving them just one,
let's do at max three vouchers per person.

420
00:26:16,199 --> 00:26:18,243
Then, implement a referral system.

421
00:26:19,536 --> 00:26:22,205
Pretty soon, the whole school
will be a gambling den.

422
00:26:24,249 --> 00:26:27,669
I'm sure you have an office or whatever.
Let's go there, have coffee, and talk.

423
00:26:27,752 --> 00:26:29,170
- [Gil-su sighs]
- How's that?

424
00:26:34,593 --> 00:26:36,595
[laughs]

425
00:26:39,514 --> 00:26:41,558
This little <i>hyeong's </i>ambitious.

426
00:26:41,641 --> 00:26:44,269
[sighs] Okay, hop in.

427
00:26:44,352 --> 00:26:45,979
Hey, take the wheel.

428
00:26:46,062 --> 00:26:47,647
- [boy 1] Sure, <i>hyeong.</i>
- [Yeong-i] <i>Oppa.</i>

429
00:26:50,233 --> 00:26:53,903
Should we wait up for the other two
and take them with us, just in case?

430
00:26:57,115 --> 00:26:58,158
Yeah, sure.

431
00:26:59,409 --> 00:27:02,329
Seong-chan, get in.
The youngest is coming with me.

432
00:27:05,582 --> 00:27:06,625
Move it.

433
00:27:08,126 --> 00:27:10,086
- [car door slides open]
- [Yeong-i sighs]

434
00:27:11,046 --> 00:27:12,881
[Su-ho] Oh!

435
00:27:13,632 --> 00:27:14,883
[sighs]

436
00:27:15,550 --> 00:27:16,468
[boy 2 grunts]

437
00:27:19,971 --> 00:27:21,264
[chuckles]

438
00:27:21,348 --> 00:27:22,682
[Su-ho exhales]

439
00:27:22,766 --> 00:27:24,142
[engine starts]

440
00:27:34,027 --> 00:27:35,403
What's that about?

441
00:27:35,487 --> 00:27:36,988
[gasps]

442
00:27:41,242 --> 00:27:42,077
Hold on a minute.

443
00:27:44,871 --> 00:27:48,208
- [Si-eun] They went to your place, right?
- Uh-huh. Why's he going there alone?

444
00:27:48,291 --> 00:27:50,710
- You're not reporting from here?
- We'll bring the police there.

445
00:27:50,794 --> 00:27:52,212
- What's the address?
- [Yeong-i sighs]

446
00:27:52,295 --> 00:27:54,923
17-1 Sanggye-ro, Nowon-gu, Seoul.

447
00:27:55,006 --> 00:27:57,050
It's a single-family house
with blue gates.

448
00:27:57,133 --> 00:27:59,260
17-1 SANGGYE, NOWON, SEOUL
HOUSE WITH BLUE DOOR

449
00:28:07,060 --> 00:28:09,187
[Beom-seok] Hey, taxi. Taxi!

450
00:28:14,567 --> 00:28:15,735
[watch buzzes]

451
00:28:18,154 --> 00:28:20,657
SI-EUN: IF THE ADDRESS IS RIGHT
TEXT ANYTHING BACK

452
00:28:25,036 --> 00:28:26,955
[Si-eun] Hey, hey. What are you doing?

453
00:28:27,038 --> 00:28:28,331
[sighs]

454
00:28:28,415 --> 00:28:30,792
Everything's gonna be okay
once I bring the money to him.

455
00:28:30,875 --> 00:28:32,752
Why's Su-ho going there alone?

456
00:28:32,836 --> 00:28:34,045
That guy's crazy.

457
00:28:34,838 --> 00:28:37,173
What are we gonna do?
What if something happens?

458
00:28:39,676 --> 00:28:41,803
Please go to 17-1 Sanggye-ro, Nowon-gu.

459
00:28:54,315 --> 00:28:55,483
[sighs]

460
00:28:55,567 --> 00:28:56,526
[Seok-dae] Yeong-a.

461
00:28:57,444 --> 00:28:58,528
What are you doing?

462
00:29:00,196 --> 00:29:01,197
[Yeong-i sighs]

463
00:29:03,074 --> 00:29:03,908
[sighs]

464
00:29:05,201 --> 00:29:07,078
Trying to make sure Gil-su goes to prison.

465
00:29:07,162 --> 00:29:08,204
What?

466
00:29:09,998 --> 00:29:12,333
He's gonna bring the police
over to our place.

467
00:29:17,297 --> 00:29:19,215
If we keep going like this,

468
00:29:20,341 --> 00:29:22,886
we're gonna be stuck
in this kind of life forever.

469
00:29:24,387 --> 00:29:26,097
You don't want that either, right?

470
00:29:36,566 --> 00:29:37,901
[Su-ho sighs]

471
00:29:39,903 --> 00:29:42,197
Stay here for a little bit, okay? Huh?

472
00:29:42,280 --> 00:29:43,782
Yeah, no problem.

473
00:29:45,241 --> 00:29:46,201
[car door opens]

474
00:29:47,202 --> 00:29:48,745
- [Su-ho] Aah.
- [car door slams]

475
00:29:51,414 --> 00:29:52,957
[ominous music playing]

476
00:29:57,962 --> 00:29:59,214
[Su-ho sighs]

477
00:30:03,676 --> 00:30:06,221
Wow, that's a pretty house.

478
00:30:07,013 --> 00:30:09,015
Blue gates. Hmm.

479
00:30:09,724 --> 00:30:11,142
That's cobalt blue, right?

480
00:30:13,436 --> 00:30:14,521
How pretty.

481
00:30:20,860 --> 00:30:21,986
[Gil-su] Let's go.

482
00:30:24,489 --> 00:30:26,491
[tense music playing]

483
00:30:34,374 --> 00:30:35,250
[Gil-su sighs]

484
00:30:38,503 --> 00:30:40,505
[distant sirens blaring]

485
00:30:42,799 --> 00:30:43,883
[Gil-su sighs]

486
00:30:44,509 --> 00:30:45,426
[Su-ho sighs]

487
00:30:46,594 --> 00:30:48,346
Sit over there. Sit. [chuckles]

488
00:30:49,389 --> 00:30:50,390
[gate closes]

489
00:30:50,473 --> 00:30:52,267
Ah, I like your place.

490
00:30:52,350 --> 00:30:54,060
- I'm into retro.
- [Gil-su chuckles]

491
00:30:54,143 --> 00:30:55,270
Something to drink?

492
00:30:55,854 --> 00:30:58,606
I'd be grateful with
just a cup of water or something.

493
00:30:59,232 --> 00:31:00,233
[Gil-su] Water?

494
00:31:03,528 --> 00:31:05,530
Hey, give your phone to me.

495
00:31:10,326 --> 00:31:13,538
- Why?
- Ah, I just want to make sure.

496
00:31:13,621 --> 00:31:15,498
This, this, this, here.

497
00:31:15,582 --> 00:31:17,917
